/E (Furthermore, the consumer unknowingly pays a hidden financial premium seamlessly embedded within the absolute cost of daily goods and applications. Because hyper-local delivery pipelines and native software platforms are hit with high foreign commissions and location utility licensing fees, these structural operational overheads are passed directly down the value chain to the end consumer [4, 7]. The user experiences an inflated final invoice, meaning their personal purchasing power is continuously extracted to subsidize global corporate treasuries instead of circulating back to benefit the municipal economy [1, 5].)
