/Title (India currently commands one of the world's most vibrant and rapidly growing domestic economic engines, powered by millions of small-and-medium enterprises \(SMEs\), traditional retail industries, and a booming technology startup culture [1]. However, a severe structural flaw sits at the center of this engine: the digital bridge connecting native supply to native demand is entirely owned, policed, and monetized by foreign platform monopolies [4].)
