740 0 obj
<<
/Title (Right now, local Indian businesses are stuck in a costly loop [3, 7]. To talk to or find customers who live in their very own cities, they have to pay a continuous "ad rent" to foreign servers [3]. This constant spending eats directly into the profit margins of our startups and small shops, leaving them with less money to grow or hire local workers [1, 7].)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 690 0 R
/Next 741 0 R
>>
endobj
741 0 obj
<<
/Title (Because these platforms are owned by foreign companies, local Indian business hubs are completely vulnerable [4]. When a tech company in Silicon Valley changes its search algorithms or ranking rules, a local market cluster in Mumbai or Bangalore can lose its online visibility and customer foot traffic within a single day [2]. This setup causes billions of rupees to leave India's economy every year [3, 4].)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 690 0 R
/Prev 740 0 R
>>
endobj
